# Snakes and Ladders Multiplayer Game

## Project Description

This project is a multiplayer Snakes and Ladders game developed using Java socket programming. The system follows a client-server architecture where the server runs on AWS EC2 and two clients connect to the server using the AWS public IP address.

The game includes:

* Multiplayer gameplay
* Turn-based system
* Snake and ladder mechanics
* Replay functionality
* Start screen and end screen
* Username system
* Graphical user interface using Java Swing
* Real-time synchronization between players

---

# Technologies Used

* Java
* Java Swing
* TCP Socket Programming
* AWS EC2 Ubuntu Server
* Git & GitHub
* NetBeans IDE

---

# Project Structure

```text
src/
│
├── client/
│   └── GameClient.java
│
├── server/
│   └── GameServer.java
│
├── common/
│   ├── Message.java
│   └── GameState.java
│
└── ui/
    ├── GameBoard.java
    └── StartScreen.java
```

---

# How to Run the Project

## 1. Start AWS Server

Connect to AWS EC2 Ubuntu instance and run:

```bash
cd SnakesAndLaddersNetwork
javac src/*/*.java
java -cp src server.GameServer
```

The server will start on port 5000.

---

## 2. Run Client Application

Open the project in NetBeans or any Java IDE and run:

```text
client.GameClient
```

Run two clients for multiplayer gameplay.

---

# AWS Configuration

* AWS Service: EC2
* Operating System: Ubuntu Server 24.04 LTS
* Server Type: t2.micro
* Communication Protocol: TCP
* Open Port: 5000

Clients connect using the AWS public IPv4 address.

---

# Game Rules

1. The game is played between two players.
2. Players roll dice in turns.
3. Ladders move the player upward.
4. Snakes move the player downward.
5. The first player reaching square 100 wins.
6. The game can be restarted without closing the application.

---

# Features

* Multiplayer network communication
* AWS cloud server support
* Modern graphical interface
* Real-time game updates
* Replay system
* Username support
* Turn restriction system
* Server-side game management

